{"theory":"wzw-models","member":{"at":"(E_7)_1"},"chiral_algebra":"(\\widehat{\\mathfrak{e}}_7)_1","Z_tex":"Z = |\\chi_{\\mathbf{1}}|^2 + |\\chi_{\\mathbf{56}}|^2","character_tex":"Weyl-Kac characters at $z = 0$: $\\chi_\\lambda(q) = \\eta(q)^{-\\dim G}\\sum_{\\beta\\in Q^\\vee}\\prod_{\\alpha>0}\\frac{(\\alpha,\\lambda+\\rho+K\\beta)}{(\\alpha,\\rho)}\\,q^{|\\lambda+\\rho+K\\beta|^2/2K}$, $K = k + h^\\vee$, long roots of length$^2$ 2 (here $\\dim G = 133$, $h^\\vee = 18$, $K = 19$). One block per integrable highest weight, labelled by the $E_7$ irrep; $h_{\\mathbf{1}} = 0$, $h_{\\mathbf{56}} = \\tfrac{3}{4}$.","description":"Diagonal modular invariant of the $E_7$ WZW model at level 1, $c = k\\dim G/(k+h^\\vee) = 7$. Characters from the Weyl-Kac formula specialised to $z=0$ (the finite Weyl sum becomes the Weyl dimension factor and the denominator becomes $\\eta^{\\dim G}$ by the Macdonald identity), summed exactly over the coroot lattice. The generator checks the Macdonald identity, the leading terms $\\dim\\lambda\\, q^{h_\\lambda-c/24}$ and that the weight-1 space of the vacuum module has dimension $\\dim G = 133$, and compares with independent formulas: $E_7$ root-lattice theta functions $\\Theta_{\\lambda+Q}/\\eta^7$.","generator":"scripts/spectra/gen_wzw.py","c":"7","irreducible":true,"cutoff":"10","s_error":4.5e-16,"gap":"1","blocks":[{"label":"\\chi_{\\mathbf{1}}","h":"0","coeffs":[1,133,1673,11914,63252,278313,1070006,3711557,11862767,35449519,100109807,269347120,694806959]},{"label":"\\chi_{\\mathbf{56}}","h":"3/4","coeffs":[56,968,7504,42616,194768,772576,2742040,8933456,27113928,77600936,211181880,550258520]}],"n_blocks":2,"primaries":[{"h":"0","hb":"0","mult":1,"pairs":[[0,0,1]]},{"h":"3/4","hb":"3/4","mult":1,"pairs":[[1,1,1]]}],"virasoro":[["0","0",1],["0","1",133],["1","0",133],["3/4","3/4",3136],["0","2",1539],["1","1",17689],["2","0",1539],["3/4","7/4",51072],["7/4","3/4",51072],["0","3",10108],["1","2",204687],["2","1",204687],["3","0",10108],["3